{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "veil_shards",
  "description": "translucent veils of light broken into curved shards: panes cut along the set's level lines and across them along bent field lines, each a soft scoop with a hard bright rim, crossing veils from four turned views",
  "reference": {
    "image": "wallhaven_wallhaven-r7ev9m.png",
    "folder": "fractal-drive-sync/style-refs",
    "made_with": "a flame fractal render (Apophysis-style), 1920x1200"
  },
  "suggested_colormap": "veil_shards",
  "reuses": [
    "soft_veils' turned views (four of its five, zoom 0.5 to 0.9) and its rank sheets of the smooth count, masked by the inverted `de`",
    "the field-lines channel (`lines`, star_eye's) at a twist, so its cuts bend into arcs"
  ],
  "adds": [],
  "notes": [
    "From wallhaven-r7ev9m (item 090, triage group 12, flame veils), with wallhaven-wqg52p (bone_star) and wallhaven-kwg7v6 (silk_shards) as palette entries. The look: translucent sheets whose edges are hard bright creases meeting at cusps, so the veils read as panes of glass broken into curved quadrilaterals, brightest where they overlap, the shards repeating smaller towards the middle. No new engine member. Every cut is two sheets, as flame_veil_violet splits its veils: a soft scoop of fill in the map's middle (fill 0.15 at edge 0.3) and a thin hard rim at its top (edge 0.02). Four turned views carry the large veils (rank sheets of the smooth count, three bands); the frame's own loop carries the shards: one cut along its level lines (period 1, a ring per escape step) and one across them along the field lines (`lines`, radius 2, twist -2, divide 1.5, period 1/8), so the two rims cross into curved cells tied to the set. Everything is masked by the inverted `de` at power 3, so the panes gather round the set.",
    "What differs from soft_veils, the nearest mode (its baseline tile in both formulation rows, in this map): soft_veils' veils are soft folds with a glow of wisps; here the rims are hard creases and the shards net the frame in curved cells, which soft_veils has none of. Without the shards (f_noshards) the stack reads as large rimmed blobs: the shards are the headline.",
    "Reachable by one escape loop: no. The veils are four views (four more loops, soft_veils' accumulated density), and the shards' field lines are a loop of their own: six loops a sample, no light.",
    "Round one's readings: f_fine (the field-line cut at 1/16), f_broad (the views at twice the zoom, sheets spanning the frame), f_gilt (rims added rather than screened, so crossings burn gold), f_noshards, and s_base, the stack folded by the kaleidoscope projection into a five-point star (views at twice the zoom, the set's hair at 0.1) for wqg52p's star of veils; the fold read as a mandala of lace at a dense quintic seat and as a star only at a shallow quadratic one, and lilac_kaleidoscope's fold kept nothing in 075, so it was offered on bone_star rather than as a mode of its own (both its tiles were kept, and it became the mode veil_star in item 092). Seats: the flame family's hand-placed shallow seats (step 4's exception, the far field veils need; soft_veils' notes), the twelve with ink under 0.10 (`style scout --points --measure`: 0.0007 to 0.058); the six over it (0.12 to 0.31) drowned the panes in lace or a flat interior, as soft_veils' notes predict.",
    "Tone: the reference's 0.350/0.235 holds at all twelve location seats and both formulation seats as shipped (p90 0.516 to 0.595 against 0.551). bone_star (0.405/0.250) and silk_shards (0.135/0.093, thin fills at 0.1, rims at 0.75, the field-line cut at 1/16) hold at both formulation seats.",
    "Explorer cost (090, round one, nothing else running): 52 s as WebAssembly on one thread at 1280x800 ss2 at its deeper formulation seat (vm_d4, maxiter 800; 49 s at vj_d3), under the 5-minute bar; 84 s at the deepest location seat offered (phoenix_2d843082, maxiter 9,266).",
    "Matt (2026-11-26): the flame veils are \"very good\", 5/5. Kept f_broad and f_gilt at both seats, locations vs_loc_05 and vs_loc_16, and bone_star and silk_shards at both seats. The star fold's two keeps (s_base, and bone_star at the quadratic star seat) became their own mode, veil_star (item 092).",
    "Published stack set to its kept reading (Matt, 2026-11-26, the lever rule; item 094): the default is f_broad, the four views at twice the zoom (1.0, 1.218, 1.484, 1.806), so the card's Example draws its kept tile. bone_star and silk_shards were kept on the old default, so each carries the old zooms (0.5 to 0.903) as values; f_gilt (both seats, rims added rather than screened) and the kept locations vs_loc_05 and vs_loc_16 were drawn at the old zooms too, and no entry now reproduces those four."
  ],
